        "date": "2026-11-13T22:26:09Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(contour)!: climb milling runs climb - outside clockwise, inside counter-clockwise with M3\n\nWith a right-hand (M3) spindle, climb milling keeps the material on the\nRIGHT of the tool's travel: an outside profile runs clockwise, an inside\nprofile counter-clockwise, and control compensation is G41. The 2D\nContour family called \"material on the left\" climb, so every contour\nposted with the default climb flag was conventional-milled.\n\n- contour: ring travel follows `climb == inside`; the air side (leads,\n  fillets, arc entries) and G41/G42 follow the corrected travel; the\n  comp room's arc law reads the tool side from the travel.\n- each ring keeps its seam; climb and conventional differ only in\n  direction (ring::walked).\n- a keep-down ring-to-ring link is proved against both rings' leads too.\n- the open-boundary contour hands its run on material-right.\n- 2D Chamfer takes the side: boss edge CW, bore edge CCW under climb.\n- cl: a vertical arc's Z-extremum split at an off-lattice end no longer\n  leaves a sub-micron sliver.\n- 2D Pocket wall pass already ran climb: pinned, not changed.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: posted G-code of every 2D Contour and 2D Chamfer\nreverses direction (G41/G42 swap under control/wear compensation); a\nproject that set climb: false as a workaround now posts conventional.\n\nFixes #1555\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
